Objectives

1. To represent a sensor network using a weighted graph.
2. To understand vertices, edges, and edge weights.
3. To implement Prim’s algorithm in C++.
4. To construct a Minimum Spanning Tree with minimum total communication cost.
5. To display the selected communication links and their weights.
6. To calculate the total cost of the Minimum Spanning Tree.
7. To identify disconnected sensors when the graph is not fully connected.
